1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Suzanne Diodati''' was from a distinguished Italian Calvinist family who had sought refuge in Geneva. She was born in 1573, exact location is disputed. Her parents were Pompee Diodati and Laura Calandrini. Her c
2 CONC ousin Jean Diodati was a famous Bible translator, a dangerous occupation in those days of religious intolerance. The Diodati family still ranks among Geneva's prominent academic families.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suzanne married Jean-Baptiste de Saussure in 1597. He was the son of Jean de Saussure and wife Catherine de Veillet. The de Saussures were an early Huguenot family from Lorraine who were living in exile in Geneva.
