1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Image at https://artuk.org/discover/artworks/david-papillon-15811659-80450
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Papillon''' (1581–1659) was a French Huguenot architect and military engineer in England
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born in France on 14 April 1581 into a Huguenot family
2 CONT * Son of Thomas Papillon, captain of the guard and valet-de-chambre to Henri IV of France, and his wife Jeanne Vieue de la Pierre. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Papillon married twice. His '''first wife''' (m. 1611, d. 1614) was Marie, daughter of Jean Castel, probably pastor, as Papillon was deacon, of the French church in London. His '''second wife''' (m. 4 July 1615) was Anne Marie, gr
2 CONC anddaughter of Giuliano Calandrini, a convert to the reformed faith, who migrated from Lucca to Lyons between 1557 and 1567, and died at Sedan some time after the massacre of St. Bartholomew.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1588 his mother sailed with him and his two sisters for England. Their ship was wrecked off Hythe; the mother died, but the children were saved. He was brought up in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parliamentarian of the English Civil War,
2 CONT Treasurer of Leicestershire from 1642 to 1646.
2 CONT Fortified Leicester and Gloucester for the parliament, and advised on the defence of Northampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death in March 1659, a memorial to Papillon was placed in St Katherine Coleman, London
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References and further reading'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Papillon,_David
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/262105003/david-papillon
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Papillon_(architect)
