1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Cesar de Saussure''' was the son of Elie de Saussure and wife Sara Burlamacchi. He was born in Geneva, Switzerland on August 31, 1637 and died on May 10, 1703. He married Anne Catherine Lullin on February 17, 16
2 CONC 70. She was the daughter of Jean Lullin and wife Caterina Calandrini. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cesar and Anne Catherine had seventeen children in twenty-two years. Most did not live to adulthood. Their eldest son's line, (Jean born 1671), died out in the early part of the next century. The next son, Theodore (1674-1750), ha
2 CONC d a distinguished career as a magistrate in Geneva. He married and had several children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Cesar de Saussure and wife Anne Catherine Lullin:
2 CONT *Jean de Saussure, born in 1671, died early in next century
2 CONT *Sarah de Saussure, 1673-1673, lived only 26 weeks
2 CONT *Theodore de Saussure, 1674-1750, married Marie Mallet (1678-1741) and had six children
2 CONT *Francoise de Saussure, 1676-1727
2 CONT *Pierre de Saussure, 1677-1677, died at five months
2 CONT *Catherine de Saussure, born 1682
2 CONT *Sarah de Saussure, 1683-1698, named for her dead sister
2 CONT *Isaac de Saussure, 1685-1701
2 CONT *Leonard de Saussure, 1686-1687, died as an infant
2 CONT *Alexandrine de Saussure, 1688-1690, died at age two
2 CONT *Cesar de Saussure, born c.1689, died 1692 at age three
2 CONT *Elie de Saussure, 1692-1716
2 CONT *Simone de Saussure, 
2 CONT *Anne de Saussure,  
2 CONT *Madeleine de Saussure,
