1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 MAY 1779
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac Mallet settled in Paris in 1711, where he represented the interests of Gédéon Mallet, one of his relatives, a holder of claims on the Royal Treasury, as a proxy for the firm "Gédéon Mallet, Cramer et Cie".
2 CONT
2 CONT Two years after his arrival in the French capital, he founded a banking house in Paris with his cousin Antoine de La Rive, from which he separated in 1718,  preferring to remain a commission banker. The bank then took the name of 
2 CONC "Isaac Mallet et Cie", then, in association with his brother-in-law Robert Dufour, the name of "Dufour et Mallet".
2 CONT
2 CONT He became a member of the Conseil des Deux-Cents in 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of the banker Jacques Mallet (1724-1815) (himself father of Guillaume Mallet and Isaac Mallet (1763-1815)).
