1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/44028391/louis-mcpherson-desaussure Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 3 2020, 23:49:49 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Henry William DeSaussure
2 CONT Mother: Elizabeth Ford
2 CONT 1825 - A.B. degree, South Carolina College, Columbia, SC
2 CONT 1827-1828  - Attended, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC
2 CONT 1828 - M.D. degree, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC (from: Columbia, SC; preceptor: Dr. Davis; thesis: "On Mania a Potu")
2 CONT 11/15/1832 - Married, Isabel Harper Means, St. Helena Parish, SC (she died in 1844)
2 CONT 01/16/1844 - Wife, Isabel, died
2 CONT 08/28/1845 - Married, Jane Hay Hutson (she died in 1887)
2 CONT 01/28/1862 - As a civilian, sold corn to the Confederate States Army, Tomotley, Beaufort District, SC
2 CONT 08/11/1862 - As a Civilian, he filed a schedule of property totaling $25,590, "lost by reason of the invasion of the enemy", at Beaufort, St. Helena Parish, SC, in November, 1861. On the schedule are thirteen slaves who are noted 
2 CONC to have "gone over to the Yankees."
2 CONT 07/31/1863 - Appointed Surgeon, Provisional Army of the Confederate States
2 CONT 08/00/1863 - Surgeon, 4th SC Troops
2 CONT 10/31/1863 - Surgeon, 4th SC Troops, Georgetown, SC
2 CONT 11/16/1863 - Granted leave of absence [S.O. 214/1  Dept. of S.C, Ga., & Fla.  - Gen. Trapier]
2 CONT 12/10/1863 - Ordered to attend the sick of the 4th Regiment South Carolina State Troops [S.O. 238/3  Dept. of S.C., Ga., & Fla.  - Gen. Trapier]
2 CONT 12/31/1863 - Surgeon, 4th SC Troops, Camp Witherspoon [near Georgetown, SC]
2 CONT 02/00/1864 - Surgeon, 4th SC Troops        
2 CONT 06/06/1869 - Died, Camden, Kershaw Co., SC 
2 CONT
2 CONT This biographical sketch is from:
2 CONT Hambrecht, F.T. & Koste, J.L., Biographical
2 CONT register of physicians who served the
2 CONT Confederacy in a medical capacity. 
2 CONT 12/27/2014. Unpublished database.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/44028391/louis_mcpherson-desaussure Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 29 2026, 6:31:06 UTC'
