1 NAME Charles /Mallet/
2 GIVN Charles
2 _MARNM Mallet
1 NAME Charles /Mallet/
2 GIVN Charles
2 SURN Mallet
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 OCT 1815
2 PLAC Jouy-en-Josas, 78
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 APR 1902
2 PLAC Paris 8ème
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Banker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.genea-bdf.org/BasesDonnees/genealogies/mallet.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2984974/pdf/eugenrev00309-0054a.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT https://museeprotestant.org/en/notice/charles-mallet-1815-1902-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Mallet was first an associate, then the chairman of the Protestant bank Mallet Frères & Cie which played  a major role in industrial development both in France and abroad during the second half of the 19th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles was the chairman of the Mallet Bank in its heyday 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Mallet was born in 1815, heir to a traditionally protestant family. He was the son of Jules Mallet and Emilie Oberkampf, and thus the grandson of Guillaume Mallet and of Christophe Oberkampf. He married his first cousin Lu
2 CONC cie, the daughter of Baron James Mallet
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles plaid an important part in the world of finance, first as associate, later as chairman of the bank at the time of its participation in the creation of numerous business ventures : with the Péreire brothers, he founded the 
2 CONC Compagnie Générale Maritime (Transatlantique).
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles also became a member of the board of directors of the PLM (Paris Lyon Méditerranée) railway company and he was to be appointed chairman in 1879. He collaborated in the creation of the Crédit Agricole and became one of its 
2 CONC directors.
2 CONT
2 CONT He encouraged the opening of the Bank Mallet to overseas ventures. In 1862 he took part in the creation of the Imperial Ottoman Bank which was to undertake the placing of a £ 6 million loan. This bank, whose Paris committee was ch
2 CONC aired by Charles Mallet, helped to promote the influence of France in the Middle East. He likewise headed the Austrian Railway Network.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1902, at the age of 87
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/pevelyne?lang=en&p=charles&n=mallet Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 26 2024, 12:50:35 UTC''
