1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=DeSaussure+&GSfn=Henry&GSmn=William&GSby=1836&GSbyrel=in&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=28720572&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Civil War veteran of the 1st South Carolina Artillery, 1st Regiment Company I and 9th Regiment of the South Carolina Infantry. He joined the Charleston Light Dragoons, and became surgeon of Major Trenholm's brigade. When this brig
2 CONC ade was was transferred to Virginia, he was, on account of his health, detailed to look after the hospitals on the coast. At one time he was also a member of the 4th Regiment of South Carolina Cavalry (Rutledge's).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the husband of Nannie W. Bostick, daughter of B. H. Bostick, Esq. They married at Robertsville Church, Beaufort District, SC on August 4, 1859.
