1 NOTE {geni:about_me} L. W. "Whit" Boykin (1861-1932), a planter, land appraiser and well-known sportsman of the Boykin community just outside Camden, South Carolina, along with his kinsmen the Canteys, experimented with many breeds to 
2 CONC resolve the problems posed by their Wateree hunting trips. With selective breeding and a little luck, Boykin developed a small multipurpose retriever now known as the Boykin spaniel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boykin_Spaniel
