1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Photo Angel®
2 CONT Stewart Bigford  · 
2 CONT tnsSrodeopfaf639t2
2 CONT
2 CONT   · 
2 CONT Several weeks ago I purchased a large 4" 3-ring binder at an estate sale. It is just absolutely FULL (literally hundreds!) of old photos - some dating as far back as 1854 to mid 1950s, documents, newspaper clippings, magazine arti
2 CONC cles, hand written family histories, typed family histories, lineages with sources, original poetry and music written by some of the people in this binder, etc. Everything is documented with hand written notes, all pics have names
2 CONC /dates/locations written on the back - AMAZING. Prominent names included Stroud, Parker, Palmer, Blanding, McFadden, just way too many to list. This entire book had so many names it was too difficult to look for any one descendant
2 CONC /family, so I contacted the Ellis County Museum/Historical Society (Ellis County, TX), where this family settled after several decades in VA and SC. They were very interested, so I hand delivered it and the currator and I spent at
2 CONC  least an hour going over all the wonderful history in this binder, she knew almost all the family names and many of those family names are still prominent in the county. For those who know their Indian Wars history, they are even
2 CONC  related to Quanna Parker the last War Chief of the Comanche Nation. Anyway, she is going to contact other historians in the county and they will see what they really have, she said it could take them months. Here are a few images
2 CONC  from the binder.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Facebook The Photo Angel 9 th of jan 2025
