1 NAME Jasper Julian /Baring-Gould/
2 GIVN Jasper Julian
2 _MARNM Baring-Gould
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 22 OCT 1920
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 NOV 1941
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jasper Julian Baring-Gould was born in England in 1920 while his father was on leave from his duties in Sarawak. Like  his brother, in late 1939, Jasper enlisted into the ranks of His Majesty's Armed forces, and ch
2 CONC ose to serve in the ranks of the Army. After Basic Training, Jasper sought to serve in the ranks of the Royal Tank Regiment. Once he completed his training for the Royal Tank Regiment, Jasper was posted to the 42nd Royal Tank Regi
2 CONC ment, after their return to Britain from Northern France in 1940. Within a few weeks, Jasper, along with his regiment, was posted to the North African campaign.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 18th November 1941, the British 8th Army unleashed the risky plan to relieve the besieged British Garrison at Tobruk, named Operation Crusader,  The 42nd Royal Tank Regiment (RTR) was part of the 22nd Armoured Brigade, 7th 
2 CONC ("Desert Rats") Armoured Division. The role of the 42nd RTR was to support the main effort of the operation, and attempt to break through the German lines, and enter Tobruk. Jasper and his fellow soldiers would push back the Germa
2 CONC n Afrika Corps within the first few days of the operation.
2 CONT
2 CONT But on the 22nd of November, Rommel ordered the 21st Panzers to counter-attack and push back the remnants  of the 22nd Brigade. By the 25th of November, the 22nd Brigade had suffered major losses, in the bitter and bloody battles 
2 CONC for the relief of Tobruk. With the loss of over 100 tanks, the British were in a desparate situation. As a counter-attack was organised by the Commander of the 7th Armoured Division, the 21st Panzers attacked once again.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jasper's tank strayed into the sights of a  Tiger tank and within moments the Tiger had fired upon the British tank, scoring a direct hit. Jasper and his crew members were killed instantly. Their bodies were laid to rest in By the
2 CONC  end of Operation Crusader on 30th December 1941, Torbruk was back within Allied control.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the close of 1941, Benjamin and Jasper’s mother Elizabeth had lost two of her sons to the war. In the wake of the Second World War, the family erected a granite plaque on one of the interior walls of St Peter’s church, Lewtrenc
2 CONC hard, dedicated to the memory of Julian Baring-Gould, and his three sons; David (who died  infancy) and Benjamin and Jasper. Below the names of Benjamin and Jasper, are the evocative and solemn words Killed in Action. A fitting tr
2 CONC ibute, to the sacrifice made by both  Benjamin and Jasper.
