1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Wayne Louis Anderegg, 81, of Reno, died Thursday in a Reno hospital.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Born April 21, 1896, in Minnesota, he came to Reno from his native state about 1921. A pharmacist, he worked throughout the area for many years.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A veteran of Army service in World War I, he was a member of the Reno BPOE and a Protestant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Gladys Smith Emerson Anderegg, died in 1956. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a daughter, Mrs. Roy Bankofier, Reno, brothers George, Fullerton, Calif, Albert, Burnsville, Minn; sister Lillian Leas, St. Paul, Minn; and a granddaughter, six great-grandchildren and one great-great-grandchild.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends may call at the O'Brien-Rogers and Crosby Funeral home in Reno today from 10 a.m. to 9 p.n. A graveside funeral is scheduled for 2 p.m. Monday in Our Mother of Sorrows Cemetery.   
2 CONT
2 CONT (Nevada State Journal, 05, Mar 1978, Pg.37)
