2 CONT James Douglas Haman (01/25/1892 - 04/13/1926)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT DR. T. L. HAMMOND [sic] DIED SUNDAY AT VAIDEN
2 CONT
2 CONT HE WAS PASTOR OF THE PRESYTERIAN CHURCH THERE FOR THE LAST FORTY YEARS
2 CONT
2 CONT  Vaiden, Nov. 4—Dr. T. L. Haman, pastor of the Presbyterian church forty years holding the longest term of continuous service in the Synod died yesterday, in his sixties. He is survived by his wife, four daughters and two sons, on
2 CONC e of the latter, Blandon Haman being now stationed Fort Olethorpe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father and builder of the famous Presbyterian school French Camp and was a member of the Board of Trustees of that Institution.
2 CONT
2 CONT His funeral will take place tomorrow. The services will be conducted by Dr. J. B. Hutton of Jackson, assisted by Dr. E T. Colmery of Edwards who is second in point to continuous service to Dr. Haman.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Winona Times – Page 3 Winona, MS November 8, 1918* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5546838/thomas-luther-haman Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 3 2020, 2
2 CONC 3:54:18 UTC''
