1 NAME Edward H /Holman/
2 GIVN Edward H
2 SURN Holman
2 _MARNM Holman
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Sumter Cemetery, Sumter, Sumter County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 NOV 1838
2 PLAC Orangeburg County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 FEB 1916
2 PLAC Abbeville, Abbeville County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 TITL Capt. (CSA),
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} son of Adam Holman and Anne Leah Wannamaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grave apparently is unmarked; photo volunteer could not find it.
2 CONT
2 CONT E H Holman
2 CONT
2 CONT Abbeville, Feb 3 [1916] - Edward H Holman died last night at the home of his daughter, Mrs J Allen Smith, Jr, after a short illness. Mr Holman was born in Orangeburg 77 years ago. He lived most of his life in Sumter but had made h
2 CONC is home in Abbeville for the past six years. He was a Confederate soldier and took a prominent part in the trying times of 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr F K Holman and Mrs T H Clark of Sumter, James H Holman of Batesburg, Mrs J A Smith and Mrs W H White of this place are his surviving children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held this morning at the late residence. The body accompanied by relatives and friends left here at 1 o'clock for Sumter where the burial will take place Friday morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb 4, 1916, The State
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT Funeral of E H Holman
2 CONT
2 CONT Sumter, Feb 4 [1916] - The body of the late Capt E H Homan of this city arrived from Abbeville and the funeral services were held this morning at the residence of his daughter, Mrs T H Clarke. Interment took place at the Sumter Ce
2 CONC metery, the services being conducted by the Rev J  Marion of the Presbyterian Church. Capt Holman was on a visit to his daughter at Abbeville when he was stricken with his last illness and passed away. He is survived by the follow
2 CONC ing children: Capt James B Holman, Batesburg; Dr Frank A Holman, Sumter; Mrs T H Clarke, Sumter; Mrs Joel Allen Smith and Mrs William White, Abbeville. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Feb 5, 1916 The State* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/119209913/edward-h-holman Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 4 2020, 0:15:00 UTC''
