1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://projects.militarytimes.com/citations-medals-awards/recipient.php?recipientid=103205 militarytimes....] ; [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=31212620 findagrave...] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Edward Harleston deSaussure , Jr.===
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward deSaussure '''Brigadier General''',  graduated from the U.S. Military Academy at West Point, Class of 1941. He retired as a U.S. Army Major General. He was Awarded the '''Distinguished Service Medal''' for actions during th
2 CONC e Vietnam War
2 CONT
2 CONT The President of the United States of America, authorized by Act of Congress July 9, 1918, takes pleasure in presenting the Army Distinguished Service Medal to Brigadier General Edward Harleston deSaussure, Jr. (ASN: 0-23790), Uni
2 CONC ted States Army, for exceptionally meritorious and distinguished services to the Government of the United States, in a duty of great responsibility as Commanding General, Force Artillery, I Field Force Vietnam, in the Republic of 
2 CONC Vietnam, during the period from December 1966 to June 1967. [This award supersedes award of the Legion of Merit awarded to General de Saussure for meritorious service during the period December 1966 to June 1967, as announced in G
2 CONC eneral Orders Number 3126, Headquarters, United States Army Vietnam, dated 24 June 1967.]
2 CONT General Orders: Department of the Army, General Orders No. 46 (October 26, 1967)
