1 NAME Caroline DeSaussure /Anderson/
2 GIVN Caroline DeSaussure
2 SURN Anderson
2 _MARNM Caulfield
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 JUN 1916
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 MAR 2011
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67608911/caroline-desaussure-caulfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Caroline DeSaussure "Dessie" Anderson Caulfield, 94, of Water Valley, Died at her Home, March 28, 2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Centreville in 1916.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Caulfield was a Daughter of the Late Oliver May and Caroline DeSaussure Haman Anderson.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Graduate of Water Valley High School and Belhaven College, she Worked at the Field Cooperative Association in Jackson; and Worked for the Treasury Department and the General Accounting Office in Washington, D.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT She Worked as Clerk of the Selective Service System for Many Years; Taught School Two Years, and was Librarian for the Water Valley Public Library and Blackmur Library for Several Years.
2 CONT
2 CONT An Active Member of the First Presbyterian Church in Water Valley, she Played the Piano, Taught Sunday School, Directed the Choir, and was a Former President of the Women in the Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Honored in 2000 with the Church Service Award from Belhaven College.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Member of the Red Hat Ladies and the Literary Club, she Enjoyed Singing, Playing the Piano, Reading, Working in her Flowers, Exercising, Playing Bridge, and Visiting with Friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her Favorite Activity was Writing Poetry.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a Charter Member of the Mississippi Poetry Society and Served as President in 1988-1989.
2 CONT
2 CONT She Received Honors for her Poetry on the Local, State, and National Levels, having Recently Received the Edward B. Shearer, III Award for Artistic Achievement from the Water Valley Arts Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT She Received the Lifetime Achievement Award from the Mississippi Poetry Society in 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT She Published a Book of Poetry, "Goblet of Dreams", in 1998, Co-Edited the 75th Anniversary Anthology of the Mississippi Poetry Society, Magnolia Heart Strings in 2002, and a Second Book will be Published in the Summer, "Mother of
2 CONC  My Love".
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held Wednesday, March 30, 2011 from 6:00 P.M. until 8:00 P.M. at Seven Oaks Funeral Home in Water Valley, MS. Funeral Service will be held at 2:00 P.M. on Thursday, March 31, 2011 at First Presbyterian Church of
2 CONC  Water Valley with Bro. Harold Sprayberry Officiating. Interment will be in the Oak Hill Cemetery with Clay Ashford, Barry Caulfield, Lloyd Caulfield, Jeff Hughes, Jeff Sheets, Anthony Wade, and Rob Hembree Serving as Pallbearers.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Ashford, Aaron Baddley, J. K. Baddley, Jim Bowles, Clyde Herron and Ersel King will serve as Honorary Pallbearers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Caulfield is Survived by a Son, James Barron Caulfield, Jr.and Wife, Elizabeth, of Water Valley; Two Daughters, Mary Alice Patterson and Husband, Jim, of Waxhaw, NC; and Dorothy Helen Wiman and Husband, Richard, of Belzoni. S
2 CONC he has Eight Grandchildren whom she Adored: James Barron "Barry" Caulfield, III and Lloyd Leland Caulfield, of Water Valley; Bethany Summers Hembree and Husband, Rob, of Madison; Elizabeth Grace Sheets and Husband, Jeff, of Indian
2 CONC  Trail, N.C; Margaret Jeanne Patterson, of Charlotte, NC; Ruth Wiman Hughes and Husband, Jeff, of Belzoni; Joy Elizabeth Steenkamp and Husband, Louis, of Pretoria, South Africa; and Lindsay Caroline Wade and Husband, Anthony, of L
2 CONC ong Beach, MS; and Two Great Grandsons, Brett and Ty Hughes; and a Great Granddaughter On The Way; and Two Sisters In Law, Mrs. Helen Simpson of Memphis; and Mrs. Lela Anderson, of Clinton; and a Host of Nieces and Nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Addition to her Parents, Mrs. Caulfield was Preceded in Death by her Devoted Husband of 52 Years, James Barron Caulfield, Sr.; a Brother, Oliver May Anderson, Jr.; and a Sister Mary Adelaide Anderson Steele.
2 CONT
2 CONT Published: Tuesday, March 29, 2011, Seven Oaks Funeral Home, Water Valley, Yalobusha County, MS,
2 CONT
2 CONT Published: Tuesday, March 29, 2011, North East Miss Daily Journal, Tupelo, Lee County, MS.
