0 @I6000000010030547318@ INDI
1 NAME Elizabeth A. /Marshall/
2 GIVN Elizabeth A.
2 SURN Marshall
2 _MARNM Marion
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 OCT 1922
2 ADDR
3 CITY Columbia
3 STAE SC
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 JUN 2016
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 	A beautiful and extraordinary lady has left our lives. Elizabeth Marshall Marion died at her home on June 6. She was born in Columbia on October 17, 1922, the eldest child of Helen Bruton and John Quitman Marshall. She was educat
2 CONC ed in Columbia public schools and was the seventh generation of her family to graduate from the University of South Carolina. A proud Gamecock, she served on the Board of Visitors for University of South Carolina for sixteen years
2 CONC , presiding as chairman for six years. She was instrumental in organizing the Carolina Scholars Program.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT At the end of World War II, in May of 1945, she married William Francis Marion and moved to Greenville. She immediately became a communicant of Christ Church Episcopal, and was an active member her entire adult life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was predeceased by her husband, William Francis Marion, and by her brother, Dr. Foster Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her sister, Jane Brooks Mays of Columbia; her brother, John Quitman Marshall of Columbia; daughters, Helen Molten and husband, Richard of Columbia and Mary Burnet Johnston and her husband Ellis; sons, Francis Ma
2 CONC rion, Jr. and wife Beverly, and Alex Marion and wife Kathy all of Greenville. She has ten grandchildren, three step-grandchildren, eleven great-grandchildren (with more to come!), many nieces and nephews, and numerous cousins, all
2 CONC  of whom she took time to know.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Grinny” attributed her longevity to “a puzzle a day, an apple a day, a nap a day, a walk a day.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral: Christ Church Episcopal, Greenville with burial following in the Church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
